<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nedunjeliyan II</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Talaiyalanganattu Seruvendra Nedunjeliyan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nedunjeliyan II was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> king of the Sangam age in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, celebrated for his victory at Talaiyalanganam over the Chera and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> kings and five chieftains. Sangam poems such as the Maduraikkanci, which describes his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a>, praise his reign. He is usually placed around the 2nd century CE.</p></div>
